From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Deliver D-Bus signals to QML with Qt 6

Two things stop a signal reaching a function in a DBusInterface on Qt 6. No
QML installed on LuneOS listened to a signal until now, so neither showed.

signalHandler() passes each argument as its own type. An untyped parameter
of a QML function is a QVariant, and QMetaMethod::invoke() will not convert:
"cannot convert formal parameter 0 from QString", and nothing is called.
Qt 5 passed QVariant for all of them. Pass QVariant where the function
declares that, and the value itself where it has typed the parameter. To
know which, the method is looked up first.

demarshallDBusArgument() tested "userType() == typeId()" for "already a
built-in type". On Qt 5 that compared with type(), which is UserType for
anything else. On Qt 6 both are the same number, so everything looks built in,
and a dict arrives in QML as an opaque QDBusArgument with nothing in it.

Checked with the plugin on a private bus against a service emitting (ssa{sv}):
without the first change the function is not called, without the second
it gets an empty object, with both it gets the strings and a plain object.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/nemo-dbus/dbus.cpp b/src/nemo-dbus/dbus.cpp
index 6d9e255..30414a7 100644
--- a/src/nemo-dbus/dbus.cpp
+++ b/src/nemo-dbus/dbus.cpp
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ QVariant demarshallDBusArgument(const QVariant &val, int depth)
             lst << QVariant::fromValue(static_cast<quint8>(arr[i]));
         res = QVariant::fromValue(lst);
 #if (QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0))
-    } else if (type == val.typeId()) {
+    } else if (type < QMetaType::User) {
 #else
     } else if (type == val.type()) {
 #endif
diff --git a/src/plugin/declarativedbusinterface.cpp b/src/plugin/declarativedbusinterface.cpp
index 7cc6a80..17b42d5 100644
--- a/src/plugin/declarativedbusinterface.cpp
+++ b/src/plugin/declarativedbusinterface.cpp
@@ -935,6 +935,10 @@ void DeclarativeDBusInterface::signalHandler(const QDBusMessage &message)
 
     QGenericArgument args[10];
 
+    QMetaMethod method = m_signals.value(message.member());
+    if (!method.isValid())
+        return;
+
     for (int i = 0; i < qMin(arguments.length(), 10); ++i) {
         const QVariant &tmp = arguments.at(i);
         normalized.append(NemoDBus::demarshallDBusArgument(tmp));
@@ -943,16 +947,17 @@ void DeclarativeDBusInterface::signalHandler(const QDBusMessage &message)
     for (int i = 0; i < normalized.count(); ++i) {
         const QVariant &arg = normalized.at(i);
 #if (QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0))
-        args[i] = QGenericArgument(QMetaType(arg.metaType()).name(), arg.data());
+        // An untyped parameter of a QML function is a QVariant, and invoke()
+        // does not unwrap one for it: only a typed parameter takes the value.
+        if (method.parameterMetaType(i) == QMetaType::fromType<QVariant>())
+            args[i] = QGenericArgument("QVariant", &arg);
+        else
+            args[i] = QGenericArgument(QMetaType(arg.metaType()).name(), arg.data());
 #else
         args[i] = Q_ARG(QVariant, arg);
 #endif
     }
 
-    QMetaMethod method = m_signals.value(message.member());
-    if (!method.isValid())
-        return;
-
     method.invoke(this, args[0], args[1], args[2], args[3], args[4],
                   args[5], args[6], args[7], args[8], args[9]);
 }
